    example: { title: "A 6-mark Explain question, marked", body: "Question pasted in: Explain why the rate of a reaction increases when the temperature rises (6 marks). Answer pasted in: Particles move faster when it is hotter, so they collide more often and the reaction speeds up. It comes back at 2 out of 6. Marking points hit: particles gain kinetic energy; collision frequency increases. Marking points missed: more particles have energy above the activation energy; a greater proportion of collisions are therefore successful; no mention of successful collisions at all. The feedback names the real problem, which is that the answer describes rather than explains, and Explain wants a linked chain. The same student rewriting it with activation energy in the chain reaches 5. The gap was exam technique, not chemistry." },
