    example: { title: "A 30-minute trigonometry mock, and what it actually caught", body: "I set the topic to trigonometric identities, 12 questions, 30 minutes, which is close to the marks-per-minute of my real paper. One question asked me to show that (1 - cos^2 x) / sin x simplifies to sin x. I wrote sin x and moved on. The review screen counted it correct, but the reason line said the marks come from stating sin^2 x + cos^2 x = 1 first, then cancelling. That is exactly the mark I would drop in June. Two more questions went the same way: right answer, missing line of working. So the score, 10 out of 12, was the least useful thing on the page. The pattern was that I skip the identity I am quoting. That went in my error log; the score did not." },
